    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, i hear you, but saying it was a \"net positive\" sounds like you're taking a side. isn't that a pretty subjective way to look at it? if the \"benefits\" didn't actually reach the majority of the population and instead caused massive instability later on, wouldn't many economists argue the net result was actually negative or at least deeply flawed? it feels like you're framing the growth as the only thing that matters and the social fallout as just a footnote.",
